{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794421920,"nonce":"/amRlO+LzqcwFK0FyfjXLJZ0dIU=","message":"`--wasm` on `hxn build` and `hxn run` landed in 077675e.\n\nWhat it does:\n- `hl --wasm`: the adapter crate is written with `crate-type = [\"staticlib\"]`, built for wasm32-wasip1 with `-Zbuild-std=std,panic_abort` and `-C relocation-model=pic -C target-feature=+mutable-globals`, then linked by the toolchain's rust-lld into `\u003clibrary\u003e.wasm` with one `--export` per `define_prim!` resolver found in the adapter text and `--unresolved-symbols=import-dynamic`. `run` compiles the program with `-D wasm`, has Ash build it with ASH_WASM_FIBERS=1 and runs it with `ash run`.\n- `cpp --wasm`: the archive is built for wasm32-unknown-emscripten with `-C panic=abort`, haxe gets `-D wasm -D emscripten -D HXCPP_M32 -D disable_unicode_strings` with CC and CXX removed from its environment, and node runs `out/\u003cMain\u003e.js`.\n- Output goes to `\u003ctarget\u003e/hxn/\u003clibrary\u003e/hl-wasm` and `cpp-wasm`, each with its own adapter crate.\n- The flags are appended to RUSTFLAGS from the environment. Flags a user keeps in cargo config are replaced by that, as with any RUSTFLAGS.\n- A toolchain whose `rustc -vV` release is not nightly or dev is refused before cargo runs, with what to install; so is `cpp --wasm` without emcc on PATH.\n- HXN_VM names the VM for `hl` and Ash for `hl --wasm`; `cpp --wasm` ignores it and takes only `--vm`, default node.\n\nRun: tests/cli/run.sh and tests/examples/run.sh in all four modes (hl on Ash, cpp, wasm on Ash, emcc) on macOS; hl on stock HashLink on the NUC; each example's main.wasm five more times under `ash run`.\n\nOpen:\n- Not run on Linux: the rust-lld path and the side-module link there, and Emscripten.\n- HXN_VM set to a stock `hl` makes `hl --wasm` fail inside that program rather than with a message of ours.\n- Arguments after `--` are passed to `ash run`